# tests/mpx6-nvme.d/boot.golden — V1 (px75): each boot's kernel lines about NVMe,
# folded (tests/mpx6-nvme's `golden`: QEMU's firmware revision, its version, to
# `QEMU`; the books' and the shutdown's counts to `N` but errors and refusals; the
# first disk's cache numbers left out). `== SESSION LEG` (LEG `any`: both
# firmwares). Written from the lane's first runs (hasu's rig, QEMU 8.2.2, CI's)
# and read line by line against the specification's fields and QEMU's
# properties before it was kept: PCI 1b36:0010 at the slot the command line
# gives, NVMe 1.4.0, MDTS 7 (512 KiB), NN 256, MQES 2047, a volatile write cache,
# the depth asked and taken (64), the queues granted (64, or 1 under
# max_ioqpairs=1), the namespaces' blocks, nvme0n1 259:0 and every NVMe disk
# before any partition on 259.

== names any
nvme0: 1b36:0010 at 00:03.0, NVMe 1.4.0 "QEMU NVMe Ctrl" serial "paxnvme0" firmware "QEMU"; MDTS 512 KiB, 256 namespaces, 1 active, a volatile write cache; nvme0n1 (namespace 1): 131072 blocks of 512 bytes; the I/O queue pair: 64 entries (asked 64, MQES 2048), 64 SQ and 64 CQ granted, a single pair, polled; the firmware left it enabled
